# @MODULE_NAME@

## Build

From a Visual Studio x64 developer prompt, with `<sdk>` as the unzipped SDK folder:

```powershell
cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=<sdk>
cmake --build build
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
```

The package folder is `build/bin/modules/@MODULE_ID@/`. To install it, zip that folder and use **Install from .zip…** in the app.

## Licence

`module.json` says `@LICENSE@`. Open source is encouraged. For a closed-source module, read `MODULE-EXCEPTION.md` in the SDK first.
